WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am so happy that
the second season is back.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is
very exciting news --

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
you already got picked up
for season three.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, congratulations.
-Yeah. I know.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:09.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a good time.
It's a good time.
-It's a very nice time.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.713
-Season two sort of picks up
right after season one ends.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
But one of
the nice additions here

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.784
is there is now another assassin
in the show.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
For people who don't know,
you are a very effective
female assassin.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:24.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And there's another one
that joins the scene.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.693 line:92%
Do you enjoy playing, maybe,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.795 size:75% position:38%
a little bit jealous
of a new assassin?

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.530 line:92%
-Yeah, it definitely ignites

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little bit of jealousy
in Villanelle.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.035
How much competition this
assassin is going to be,

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
we will see.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't imagine it
to be too much.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.373
-Well, you're a very, like
I said, effective assassin.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.042 line:92%
And is it true that you have,

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the makeup trailer,
a kill wall?

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So this is -- Explain
the kill wall real quick.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.181
-I'm sure the actors will
be thrilled to hear this,

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the way.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so whenever
we had an actor

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.086 line:92%
who was -- who suddenly left us,

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
we would put a big red cross
through their face

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:57.624
and turn them upside down
and put them on a separate wall.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:01.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we slowly realized
that the death wall

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
was so much bigger
than the remaining cast.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So there are more dead people
on your show than living.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pretty much.
-How many -- Do you keep
internal count in your head

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
of how many people
your character has killed?

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I haven't. I haven't.
-Yeah.

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.076
It's just so meaningless to you
that it's just like,

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What does it matter?"
-Well, it's just hard to
keep tabs.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
And also, like,
we've literally

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
joined her life so late
in the game that I'm like,

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Can you imagine
all the people prior?"
-Oh, right.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:26.152
You've probably killed a lot of
people before the show started.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:28.388 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Too many to mention.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:32.125
-You -- We talked about your
family last time you were here.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
You still live in Liverpool.
-Still there.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that's where
your family's from.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do they -- Do they like
the show? Are they fans of it?

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.333 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, they love it.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, every time I come home,
my dad's got it on repeat

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on the television.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
He keeps rewatching it.
But they love it.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.707 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's so much fun.

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think they are
a little bit cautious.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.010 line:92%
Like, they sometimes look at me

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.113 size:81% position:41%
and wonder where I get
the crazy eyes from.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right.
-They're like, "Okay,

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.683 line:92%
we live with this person."

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I will even say it
myself,

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.353
but the first time I met you on
the show, not only, obviously,

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
is your accent completely
different from the character
in the show,

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you are far --
you're very nice in person.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-And you don't seem --

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's all an act.
-One of them's an act,

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:13.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm gonna
figure it out, Jodie.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.434 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Your dad works for

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.203
a professional football club
over there called Everton.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He does.
He works for Everton, yes.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so --
And I'm assuming that means,

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.242 line:92%
is he's a fan of the team?

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well he was born
in Everton,

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
like all my family are.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I used to go to the games
when I was younger.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.517 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Not so much now.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
But sometimes my dad
would get superstitious.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when I was younger, if they
were on a winning streak,

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.456 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I would have to go.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.958
Or if he had a -- you know,
if he had a beard at the time

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were winning, then
that beard would just continue

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
and continue
until they lost a game.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't want to
be too negative.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
But based on my knowledge
of Everton,

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
his beard probably
never got that long.
-It's like Dumbledore.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-No, that's so bad.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:54.107
[ Laughing ] He's gonna kill me
for saying that.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.642 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You --

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.810
This is really cool that you
did this for your parents.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.080
My family, my parents introduced
me to "Monty Python."

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have heard tell that yours
did for you, as well.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you got to introduce them
to Michael Palin.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:11.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I did a drama with
Michael when I was about 16,

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.258 line:92%
and we filmed in Yorkshire.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.394
And we were having dinner
at the hotel one night,

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:17.597
and Michael walked in, 'cause
that's where we were staying.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my dad was like,
"Do you want to ask Michael

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he wants to have dinner
with us?"

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.502 line:92%
And I was like, "Yeah, sure."

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Michael came
and had dinner with us.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.040
So, that was, like, my dad's --
-That's really great.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
And was it -- Like,
sometimes I feel like

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:32.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you have dinner
with one of your heroes,

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
you end up, like,
not actually enjoying it.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel like your dad --
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I feel he asked every
question that he ever
wanted to ask him.

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:40.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good, 'cause sometimes
I feel like you clam up

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.856
and you think, "I don't want to
be the guy to ask
those questions."

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you ruin the night
by talking to Michael Palin
about the weather.

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:49.395
-He wasn't embarrassing at all.
I was very proud of him.
-Okay, good.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-That's great.

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:52.532 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And then another thing.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:55.001
I know we have this in common
inherited from our parents.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are a huge
Bruce Springsteen fan?

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. So big.
-That's great. So...

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I knew --
-He's the best.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:03.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I knew he was worldwide,
but even -- even in Liverpool,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Boss is a big deal.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.280 line:92%
I mean, well, I actually, sadly,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.082 size:78% position:39%
couldn't get tickets
to the Broadway show.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I went.
-Yeah, I know.
You're just gonna rub that in.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Aren't you?
-I don't think I rubbed it in.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I mentioned it.
-No, I know.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.590
-I was there,
and I had very good seats. Yeah.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:23.329
-Well, in Liverpool, I was home
a couple of weeks ago.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.030 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And my best mate Liv,

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.865 size:81% position:41%
she's also a massive
Bruce Springsteen fan.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.368
And we were in a bar, and we
were the only people in there,

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was one guy
playing the guitar live.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:34.374
And Olivia surprised me and
requested Bruce Springsteen

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then got me
on her shoulders.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we had our own
Bruce Springsteen concert
in Liverpool.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.746 size:81% position:41%
-Oh, wow. I'm sorry,
I just want to go back

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make sure I got
this picture painted right.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're in an empty bar,
one singer.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-You request Springsteen.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.353
What -- Do you remember
the song, what he played?

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:51.090
-I think it was "Born to Run."
-Okay, so now "Born to Run."

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard the intro,
and I was like --

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
looked at my mate Liv,
and she was like...

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:57.230
-So even in an empty bar,
you have the enthusiasm

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
of like, "We can't miss
this opportunity."
-No.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:02.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you get on your friend's
shoulders in an empty bar.
-Yeah.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:04.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did -- how did
the bar staff react to it?

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They actually,
like, let us do it.
-Oh, really?

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.442
-Surprisingly, 'cause this
happens quite frequently,

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:11.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we usually
get told to get down.
-Yeah.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:13.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, no,
they could obviously see --

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:16.716
-I mean, I guess when you
only have two customers.

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
"On a crowded night,
we might get you out of here.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we would love
to have you stay

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, if possible,
order some food."

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:25.391 line:92%
-Yeah. That's a very good point.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations again
on the show.

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is always just so lovely
to have you back here.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks for having me.
-Come back for season three,
as well.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.799
-Absolutely.
-That's Jodie Comer, everybody.

